---
title: Sample Page
description: A kitchen sink of everything the Content field can hold.
---
This page is a Keystatic **singleton**, and its Content field shows every kind of formatting the editor supports. Edit it at [/keystatic](/keystatic) under *Sample Page*.

## Text formatting

Plain text with **bold**, *italic*, ~~strikethrough~~, `inline code`, and ***bold italic***. Links can point [inside the site](/) or [to another site](https://keystatic.com/docs).

## Headings

# Heading 1

## Heading 2

### Heading 3

#### Heading 4

##### Heading 5

###### Heading 6

## Lists

Unordered list:

- First item
- Second item
  - Nested item
  - Another nested item
- Third item

Ordered list:

1. Install dependencies
2. Run `npm run dev`
3. Open `/keystatic`
   1. Choose *Sample Page*
   2. Edit and save

## Blockquote

> Content is stored as Markdoc files in Git, so every edit has history.
>
> — The Keystatic approach

## Code block

```ts
// keystatic.config.ts
const useCloud = !import.meta.env.DEV;

export default config({
  storage: useCloud ? { kind: 'cloud' } : { kind: 'local' },
});
```

